00:00:15.980 --> 00:00:21.620
Five-term Michigan congressman Justin Amash has announced that he's running for the libertarian party's

00:00:21.620 --> 00:00:27.160
presidential nomination which will be decided in late May. The 40 year-old son of middle-eastern immigrants

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:33.600
took office in 2011 as a Republican but left the party last July saying he didn't want to be part of a

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:39.320
partisan death spiral. He's consistently voted against corporate bailout,  increases in debt finance

00:00:39.320 --> 00:00:45.340
government spending, overseas military interventions, and the prosecution of the federal drug war

00:00:45.340 --> 00:00:51.940
During the Coronavirus Pandemic Amash has castigated federal agencies, such as the CDC and FDA,

00:00:51.940 --> 00:00:56.940
first for botching containment efforts and then for asserting monopoly control over testing.

00:00:56.940 --> 00:01:04.300
He was one of a mere handful of no votes on the 2.2 trillion dollar CARES Act, arguing that all relief payments

00:01:04.300 --> 00:01:10.580
should go directly to individuals and households rather than corporations, nonprofits, or government agencies.

00:01:10.580 --> 00:01:15.620
We intend to win this race. I mean it's not a race for fun as I've said many times.

00:01:15.620 --> 00:01:22.120
Republican and Democratic loyalists are lashing out at Amash as a quixotic potential spoiler with no chance

00:01:22.120 --> 00:01:28.580
of being elected and calling for him to step aside. We do not have room for error in this election. This is no time

00:01:28.580 --> 00:01:36.260
for a Ross Perot or a Jill Stein or a Ralph Nader. Third party candidates are always a pain in the butt.

00:01:36.260 --> 00:01:41.840
But I think that Amash is going to hurt the Republicans more than the Democrats.

00:01:41.840 --> 00:01:48.640
It 100% helps Trump hurts Biden. I talked with Amash over Skype about why he thinks Donald Trump

00:01:48.640 --> 00:01:55.260
is too erratic to be given a second term, why Joe Biden is too old for a first term, and why he believes

00:01:55.260 --> 00:01:59.620
his vision of a freer country will take him to victory in November.

